    "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 22 at 10:57AM PDT until October 22 at 2:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall continues. Canyon rock and mudslides possible.\n\n* WHERE...Southern and Eastern Los Angeles County in southwestern\nCalifornia...\n\n* WHEN...Until 200 PM PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nWater over roadways. Canyon rock and mud slides possible. Minor\ndebris flows possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1056 AM PDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. This  will cause urban and small stream flooding\nand potential rock and canyon mud slides, and minor debris flows.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nLong Beach, Wrightwood, Whittier, West Covina, Glendora, San\nDimas, Pomona, Torrance, Redondo Beach, Rancho Palos Verdes, La\nVerne, Carson, Port of Los Angeles, Rolling Hills, Hacienda\nHeights, Santa Fe Springs and Norwalk.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
    "response": "Avoid",
